    "aliases": [
      "Rohilla War",
      "Battle of Miranpur Katra"
    ],
    "summary": "In 1774 Warren Hastings hired a Company brigade to the Nawab of Awadh to crush the Rohilla Afghans of Rohilkhand. The stated aim was a buffer against the Marathas; the price was a subsidy. Hafiz Rahmat Khan was killed at Miranpur Katra. Rohilkhand passed to Awadh, except Rampur. Hastings’s critics, Edmund Burke among them, charged that Company troops had been let out on hire and that atrocities against Rohilla civilians were condoned. Colonial conquest here was a paid campaign inside another Indian state’s war.",
    "scale": "medium",
    "scaleRationale": "A single-season war that redrew Rohilkhand and later became an article of Hastings’s impeachment.",
