    ],
    "summary": "Between 1799 and 1805 the Company broke the palaiyakkarars of the old Tirunelveli country. Veerapandiya Kattabomman of Panchalankurichi refused the Arcot-assigned revenue. His fort was taken; he was hanged at Kayathar on 16 October 1799. The Maruthu brothers rose in 1801. The Company razed forts, disbanded polygar armies, and turned surviving chiefs into zamindars under the Permanent Settlement. Colonial conquest in the deep south was a tax war against local military households.",
