    ],
    "summary": "From 1814 to 1816 the Company invaded the Gorkha kingdom. Early columns were beaten in the hills; Gillespie was killed at Nalapani above Dehradun. Ochterlony took the western front at Malaun in 1815 and threatened Kathmandu in 1816. The Treaty of Sugauli, ratified 4 March 1816, stripped Nepal of Kumaon, Garhwal, and much of the Tarai, placed a resident at Kathmandu, and opened Gurkha recruitment into Company service. Colonial conquest here was a Himalayan border war that also hired the defeated army.",
